form="translate(239.203125 24)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">Average Ratings of </text><text text-anchor="middle" transform="translate(239.203125 48)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">Urban Agriculture’s Contribution to </text><text text-anchor="middle" transform="translate(239.203125 72)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">Various Social or Ecological Services</text><text text-anchor="middle" transform="translate(239.203125 422.1806982421875)" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text">Group</text><rect xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" x="50.44606018066406" y="439.3406982421875" height="127" width="314.1078796386719" stroke="#000000" stroke-linejoin="mitre" stroke-width="0.9"/><rect xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x="57.44606018066406" y="451.3406982421875" height="12" width="12" fill="#666666" stroke="#000000" stroke-linejoin="mitre" stroke-width="0.9"/><text transform="translate(79.44606018066406 463.3406982421875)" text-anchor="top" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text"> provision of medicinal plants</text><rect xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x="57.44606018066406" y="483.3406982421875" height="12" width="12" fill="#CCCCCC" stroke="#000000" stroke-linejoin="mitre" stroke-width="0.9"/><text transform="translate(79.44606018066406 495.3406982421875)" text-anchor="top" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text"> improvement of neighborhood</text>,<text transform="translate(79.44606018066406 519.3406982421875)" text-anchor="top" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text"> attachment</text><rect xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" x="57.44606018066406" y="539.3406982421875" height="12" width="12" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-linejoin="mitre" stroke-width="0.9"/><text transform="translate(79.44606018066406 551.3406982421875)" text-anchor="top" fill="#000000" font-size="19.84" font-family="Crimson Text"> improvement of local microclimate</text></g></svg></figure><div class="sr-only" role="region" aria-label="Long description for bar graph titled Average Ratings of Urban Agriculture’s Contribution to Various Social or Ecological Services"><ul>
<li>For each data category, the following bars are shown:<br/>
<ul>
<li>provision of medicinal plants</li>
<li>improvement of neighborhood attachment</li>
<li>improvement of local microclimate</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>The data for the 3 categories are as follows:<br/>
<ul>
<li>project leaders:<br/>
<ul>
<li>provision of medicinal plants: 2.0</li>
<li>improvement of neighborhood attachment: 3.0</li>
<li>improvement of local microclimate: 3.0</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>stakeholders:<br/>
<ul>
<li>provision of medicinal plants: 3.6</li>
<li>improvement of neighborhood attachment: 4.1</li>
<li>improvement of local microclimate: 4.1</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>general public:<br/>
<ul>
<li>provision of medicinal plants: 4.6</li>
<li>improvement of neighborhood attachment: 4.3</li>
<li>improvement of local microclimate: 3.8</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div>
<p>Urban agriculture is the practice of growing plant- or animal-based products in urban settings such as community gardens and rooftop farms. Esther Sany&eacute;-Mengual, Kathrin Specht, and their team surveyed three groups of people in Bologna, Italy&mdash;leaders of urban agriculture projects, stakeholders in urban agriculture (<span data-ssml-sub-alias="e g">e.g.</span>, food researchers and urban farming associations), and the general public&mdash;to compare their views about the extent to which urban agriculture contributes to 25 social or ecological services that the team identified. The survey results show that, on average, project leaders rated urban agriculture as contributing less to <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span></p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice most effectively uses data from the graph to complete the assertion?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"4a6dc013-222f-40d8-a4ce-0d5fcc1743b5","content":"<p>providing medicinal plants than to improving the local microclimate.</p>"},{"id":"23551d07-3017-4f2e-a8e8-0540d33944d6","content":"<p>improving community members&rsquo; sense of attachment to the neighborhood than to offering educational opportunities.</p>"},{"id":"d97de3b3-270c-4cef-917a-a17a6db9f372","content":"<p>improving the local microclimate than to providing medicinal plants.</p>"},{"id":"46e059a9-4836-47ce-a307-a6aacb1f22bf","content":"<p>improving the local microclimate than to providing tourist attractions.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["4a6dc013-222f-40d8-a4ce-0d5fcc1743b5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer because it most effectively uses data from the graph to complete the assertion about urban agriculture. The graph shows the average survey ratings, on a scale of 0 to 5, from three groups of people&mdash;project leaders, stakeholders, and the general public&mdash;concerning the contributions of urban agriculture. According to the graph, project leaders gave an average rating of approximately 2 to urban agriculture&rsquo;s contributions to the provision of medicinal plants, which is lower than the average rating of approximately 3 that project leaders gave to urban agriculture&rsquo;s contributions to both improving the local microclimate and improving a sense of attachment to the neighborhood. This shows that project leaders rated urban agriculture as contributing less to providing medicinal plants than to improving the local microclimate.</p><p>Choice B is incorrect because the graph doesn&rsquo;t provide data about urban agriculture&rsquo;s contribution to educational opportunities; therefore, this comparison can&rsquo;t be made. Choice C is incorrect because it contradicts the data shown in the graph. On average, project leaders gave a rating of approximately 3 to urban agriculture&rsquo;s contributions to improving the local microclimate, which is higher, not lower, than the average rating of approximately 2 that they gave to its contributions to providing medicinal plants. Choice D is incorrect because the graph doesn&rsquo;t provide data about urban agriculture&rsquo;s contribution to providing tourist attractions; therefore, this comparison can&rsquo;t be made.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"ff18829b","external_id":"882d3996-3ca3-40a3-8e33-d2940a3ff118","vaultid":null,"uId":"81af777c-c1b9-409d-a11d-856b4bd01981","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_cd":"INI","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill_cd":"COE","skill_desc":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<figure class=\"image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"400\" height=\"577.3406982421875\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 577.3406982421875\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar graph titled Average Ratings of Urban Agriculture’s Contribution to Various Social or Ecological Services. The horizontal axis is labeled Group. 3 data categories are shown. The vertical axis is labeled Rating (0 = no contribution, 5 = high contribution). It ranges from 0 to 5 in increments of 1. Refer to long description.\"><g id=\"ed420550-79eb-48d4-af01-cd27cdd08afd\" data-name=\"Layer 1\"><defs>\n      <pattern id=\"bar4\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"10\" height=\"100\" patternUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" patternTransform=\"rotate(50)\">\n        <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"5\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#CDCDCD\"/>\n        <rect x=\"5\" y=\"0\" width=\"5\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#444444\"/>\n      </pattern>\n    </defs><line xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x1=\"93.40625\" y1=\"96\" x2=\"385\" y2=\"96\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><line xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x1=\"87.40625\" y1=\"96\" x2=\"99.40625\" y2=\"96\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><text text-anchor=\"end\" transform=\"translate(81.40625 102)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">5</text><line xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x1=\"93.40625\" y1=\"136\" x2=\"385\" y2=\"136\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><line xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x1=\"87.40625\" y1=\"136\" x2=\"99.40625\" y2=\"136\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><text text-anchor=\"end\" transform=\"translate(81.40625 142)\" fill=\"#000000\" font-size=\"19.84\" font-family=\"Crimson Text\">4</text><line xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x1=\"93.40625\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"385\" y2=\"176\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"0.9\"/><line xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" x1=\"87.40625\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"99.40625\" y2=\"176\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-linecap=\"ro